# Mintlify technical writing

You write Database Fundamentals docs in Mintlify MDX. Follow `AGENTS.md`. Start new lessons from `/templates/` (how-to, tutorial, explanation, reference). Read `docs.json` and similar pages before you add or rewrite content. Prefer searching current Mintlify docs over training data. Use the [docs.json schema](https://mintlify.com/docs.json) for site config and navigation.

## Language and style

- Second person ("you") for instructions
- Active voice; present tense for current state, future tense for outcomes
- Sentence case for headings
- One idea per sentence; parallel lists, headings, and steps
- Bold UI labels; backtick paths, commands, SQL, and identifiers
- Define jargon on first use
- No marketing language, filler, or "simply / just / easily"
- Say **table**, **row**, **column**, **primary key**, **query**; say **database** only for the whole system; prefer **schema** over **model** unless you mean an ORM
- Do not invent dialects, vendors, or features that are not on the page
- Do not document Mintlify, Cursor, or this repo on lesson pages

## Organization

- Lead with the outcome (inverted pyramid)
- Basic concepts before advanced ones
- Prerequisites before procedures
- Expected result after each major step
- Keyword-rich, descriptive headings
- Troubleshooting for likely failures
- Verification when success is not obvious

## Page structure

Every page starts with YAML frontmatter:

```yaml
---
title: "Clear, specific, keyword-rich title"
description: "What the reader can do or understand after this page"
---
```

- File names are kebab-case: `primary-keys.mdx`
- Internal links are root-relative with no extension: `/templates/how-to`
- Add every new page to `docs.json` navigation
- Body headings start at H2 (the title is H1)
- Images live in `/images`, use `<Frame>` plus descriptive alt text
- Actionable link text; never "click here"
- Code blocks always have a language tag; use realistic names (`orders`, `customer_id`), not `foo`/`bar`
- Never put real secrets in examples
- Mark unknowns with `{/* TODO: ... */}` instead of guessing
- After edits: `mint validate` and `mint broken-links`

## Component selection

- **Steps** for sequential procedures
- **Tabs** for alternative approaches or dialects
- **CodeGroup** for the same example in more than one SQL dialect or language
- **Accordions** for optional or troubleshooting detail
- **Note** extra context; **Tip** advice; **Info** neutral background; **Warning** destructive risk; **Check** success
- **Card** / **CardGroup** for linked next steps
- **ParamField** / **ResponseField** / **Expandable** for reference of clauses, arguments, and nested results
- **RequestExample** / **ResponseExample** only if you document an HTTP API
- Do not add components that only decorate the page

## Callouts

```mdx
<Note>Supporting context the reader can skip.</Note>
<Tip>A shortcut or better default.</Tip>
<Warning>Data loss, irreversible `DROP`, or breaking change.</Warning>
<Info>Neutral background, such as which SQL this example uses.</Info>
<Check>How to confirm the change worked.</Check>
```

## Code

```sql orders.sql
SELECT customer_id, COUNT(*) AS order_count
FROM orders
GROUP BY customer_id;
```

````mdx
<CodeGroup>
```sql PostgreSQL
SELECT customer_id
FROM orders
WHERE created_at >= DATE '2024-01-01';
```

```sql SQLite
SELECT customer_id
FROM orders
WHERE created_at >= '2024-01-01';
```
</CodeGroup>
````

## Structure

````mdx
<Steps>
<Step title="Create the table">
  Run the `CREATE TABLE` statement.

  <Check>Confirm the table exists in the schema listing.</Check>
</Step>
<Step title="Add the primary key">
  ```sql
  ALTER TABLE orders
  ADD CONSTRAINT orders_pk PRIMARY KEY (order_id);
  ```

  <Warning>Do not run this until duplicate `order_id` values are gone.</Warning>
</Step>
</Steps>
````

````mdx
<Tabs>
<Tab title="PostgreSQL">
  ```sql
  CREATE INDEX orders_customer_id_idx ON orders (customer_id);
  ```
</Tab>
<Tab title="SQLite">
  ```sql
  CREATE INDEX orders_customer_id_idx ON orders (customer_id);
  ```
</Tab>
</Tabs>
````

```mdx
<AccordionGroup>
<Accordion title="Query returns no rows">
  - Confirm the table has data
  - Check the `WHERE` clause types (text vs number)
</Accordion>
<Accordion title="Primary key error">
  Duplicate values in the key column block the constraint
</Accordion>
</AccordionGroup>
```

```mdx
<CardGroup cols={2}>
<Card title="About primary keys" icon="key" href="/templates/explanation">
  What a primary key is and when to use one.
</Card>
<Card title="Add a primary key" icon="list-check" href="/templates/how-to">
  Add a primary key to an existing table.
</Card>
</CardGroup>
```

## Reference fields

```mdx
<ParamField body="customer_id" type="integer" required>
  Identifies the customer. Must match `customers.customer_id`.
</ParamField>

<ResponseField name="order_count" type="integer" required>
  Number of rows in `orders` for that customer.
</ResponseField>
```

